  profileITNModal:
    '<div class="ITNHelpModal"><div class="disc-inside"><div class="ITN-title" data-i18n="profile.contact.itntitle">IP Telephony Number (ITN)</div><p data-i18n="profile.contact.itnpara1">The IP telephony number (ITN) is an internal IBM telephone number that is used to make low cost calls to IBMers worldwide from IP based telephones and from approved versions of SIP based softphones. The growth of IBM and the importance of global real-time collaboration are making the use of tie lines obsolete and all calling between IBMers will eventually be done solely with the ITN. The ITN is now in place for many users in NA, LA, EMEA and AP.</p><p data-i18n="profile.contact.itnpara2">The user can create an ITN in one of two ways:</p><p data-i18n="profile.contact.itnpara3">1) The ITN is created based on the tie line number entered by the user. The "Tie line number" field must be correct in order to have a correct ITN.</p><p data-i18n="profile.contact.itnpara4">2) The user can leave the tie line number BLANK and enter an ITN manually. This option applies when users do not have a tie line but have been provided with an ITN by their local in-country voice network administrator.</p><p data-i18n="profile.contact.itnpara5">For either 1) or 2) above, the ITN will be created only if it is globally unique. If another user already has that ITN it will not be created. Users can share a tie line number but they cannot share an ITN.</p></div></div>',
